Non-alcoholic beer is brewed to replicate the taste and drinking experience of conventional beer while containing little or no alcohol, typically less than 0.5% alcohol by volume (ABV). The category includes alcohol-free lagers, ales, wheat beers, and craft-style varieties that appeal to consumers seeking alternatives to traditional alcoholic beverages.

The market is gaining traction as consumers adopt more mindful drinking habits without giving up familiar social occasions. Brewers are expanding their alcohol-free portfolios, refining flavor profiles, and increasing distribution through mainstream retail and hospitality outlets.

Europe leads the global market, accounting for approximately 38% of market share, supported by an established beer culture and growing acceptance of alcohol-free alternatives.

